  "notes": "USAGE:\nImplies adding something supplementary rather than something essential. The added item complements or enhances the main item. Often used in contexts involving food presentation, gift-giving, and written communication.\n\nDistinct from {加|くわ}える, which means to add in a more general sense. {添|そ}える specifically suggests placing something alongside as an accompaniment.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {手|て}を{添|そ}える: to lend a hand, to place one's hand on\n- {言葉|ことば}を{添|そ}える: to add a few words\n- {花|はな}を{添|そ}える: to add flowers (as decoration); to add color to an event\n- サラダを{添|そ}える: to serve with a salad",
